# ── Neon / PostgreSQL (REQUIRED for the blog CMS) ─────────────────
# Copy the POOLED connection string from the Neon dashboard
# (Dashboard → Connection Details → "Pooled connection").
# The host MUST contain "-pooler" for serverless/Vercel deployments,
# otherwise Neon's connection limit is exhausted under load.
#
# This same variable must also be set in Vercel:
#   Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables → DATABASE_URL
#   (apply to Production, Preview AND Development, then REDEPLOY)
#
# Without it the API cannot reach the database and no blog post is ever saved.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxx-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require
